# Generated by `xforge install`, and rewritten in full by every run.
#
# It is a cache of what install wrote -- a per-file digest map for every installed target, plus the
# timestamps of the run that wrote it. Nothing in it is authored, and install can rebuild all of it
# from the Scaffold and the Manifest.
#
# Tracking it makes an ordinary team event a hard stop: two developers who each run `install` on
# their own branch conflict here as a matter of course, and a conflicted file is no longer JSON, so
# `state`, `install`, `sync` and `update` all refuse at the first read. XForge's own repository has
# ignored this file since before the Scaffold shipped one; a project scaffolded from it did not.
#
# Already tracked it? `git rm --cached xforge/.state.json` once, then commit. The file stays on
# disk and install keeps maintaining it.
.state.json
